{"type":"agent_end","messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Using this dataset's total farmers markets (excl. territories) and the 2025 population from the census file's own 'United States' row : how many farmers markets does the U.S. have per 100,000 residents, to four decimal places? One confident sentence. Do not mention unverified facts and use tools to do any math necessary. Data sources: https://harvestlymarkets.com/data/us-farmers-markets-by-state-2026.csv and https://gist.githubusercontent.com/hussainsultan/369600f5179b22792a2b4c9ed37de056/raw/NST-EST2025-ALLDATA.csv"}],"timestamp":1786912142120},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me break down what the user is asking:\n\n1. Get the total farmers markets (excluding territories) from the first dataset\n2. Get the 2025 US population from the census file's 'United States' row\n3. Calculate farmers markets per 100,000 residents to four decimal places\n\nI need to:\n1. First, check if there's a catalog and existing models/aliases\n2. If not, ingest both CSV files\n3. Calculate the metric\n4. Verify everything\n\nLet me start by checking the catalog situation and orienting myself with the available aliases and models.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"text","text":"I'll help you calculate the farmers markets per 100,000 residents. Let me start by orienting to the xorq catalog and the available data."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01DAQ64esAcKkKVNJmChR63E","name":"xorq_catalog_info","arguments":{"catalog_path":".xorq/catalog"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01WuouJrA8Z44QY7fgqdJRx9","name":"xorq_semantic_models","arguments":{"catalog_path":".xorq/catalog"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01QP6YMtv22YvMRrPE6istZS","name":"xorq_catalog_list_aliases","arguments":{"catalog_path":".xorq/catalog"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-haiku-4-5","usage":{"input":10,"output":331,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":8177,"totalTokens":8518,"cost":{"input":0.000009999999999999999,"output":0.0016550000000000002,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0.01022125,"total":0.01188625},"cacheWrite1h":0,"reasoning":134},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1786912142137,"responseId":"msg_011Ce74PwPNsAzczVB1bCmnc","rawStopReason":"tool_use"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_01DAQ64esAcKkKVNJmChR63E","toolName":"xorq_catalog_info","content":[{"type":"text","text":"path:    /private/tmp/trial-pi-52-qllulzr1/.xorq/catalog\ncommit:  07f2fe45c517\nremotes: (none)\nentries: 0\naliases: 0\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786912627289},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_01WuouJrA8Z44QY7fgqdJRx9","toolName":"xorq_semantic_models","content":[{"type":"text","text":"No semantic models in this catalog — fall back to the ordinary ingest/compose flow."}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786912627289},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_01QP6YMtv22YvMRrPE6istZS","toolName":"xorq_catalog_list_aliases","content":[{"type":"text","text":"No aliases.\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786912627289},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The catalog is empty, so I need to ingest both CSV files. Let me follow the xorq-catalog skill pattern and create build scripts to ingest the data.\n\nI need to:\n1. Ingest the farmers markets CSV\n2. Ingest the census CSV\n3. Create a metric that divides farmers markets by population * 100,000\n\nLet me start by creating the build scripts in `.xorq/scripts/`.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The catalog is empty, so I'll ingest both datasets. Let me create build scripts for each source."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01GP82JWXVi3cM6qwc5WoJ1Z","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"mkdir -p /private/tmp/trial-pi-52-qllulzr1/.xorq/scripts"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-haiku-4-5","usage":{"input":14,"output":203,"cacheRead":8177,"cacheWrite":512,"totalTokens":8906,"cost":{"input":0.000014,"output":0.001015,"cacheRead":0.00081770000